WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.960
Okay, so my 70B makes one token at a time,

2
00:00:03.960 --> 00:00:07.567
reading all its weights from memory while the compute sits idle.

3
00:00:07.567 --> 00:00:10.387
So I use speculative decoding,

4
00:00:10.387 --> 00:00:13.500
where a 1B model drafts the next few tokens.

5
00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:16.320
My 70B checks them all in one pass,

6
00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:18.900
and because the weights load once,

7
00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:22.200
that costs about the same as making one token.

8
00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:26.800
It keeps what it agrees with and fixes the first miss,

9
00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:30.060
so three right out of five gives me four tokens.

10
00:00:30.067 --> 00:00:32.887
Since my 70B has the final say,

11
00:00:32.927 --> 00:00:34.567
the output doesn't change,

12
00:00:34.567 --> 00:00:37.867
and a good draft makes it two to three times faster.
